  "protocolVersion": 1,
  "name": "A phone snapshot adds the entries it logged, under its own ids",
  "description": "The phone holds the session and logs two sets. It answers a snapshot request, then Sync runs again after it logged one more set. Its answers carry the entries it logged itself, under the ids it mints, and the wrist stores an id it does not hold while an id it already holds is not stored a second time. Structure, position, revision and timers are replaced, and entries merge by entryId, so the wrist's own observation survives the merge and the phone holds the entries its peer logged.",
